IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ssa-payments`

-- Social Security Act 1991 (Cth) -- the lost formulas the first pass took as inputs or inferred, now computed, beside
-- ssa-payments.l4 (which is left as it was).
--
-- ssa-payments.l4 asked for the age pension's two tapers (point 1064-E10 and Table G-2 column 3) as "reduction per dollar of
-- excess" inputs, took the result of point 1067G-F28 as a supplied figure, and inferred the shapes of point 1067G-F27 and
-- s 598(2A). The sidecar ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A04121.formulas.md now gives all of them:
--   * 1064-E10: reduction for ordinary income = Ordinary income excess x 0.5
--   * Table G-2 column 3 (items 1, 2 and 3 alike): reduction (per year) = Assets excess x 19.5 / 250
--   * 1067G-F27: The excess / 130 (the first pass's inference was right)
--   * 1067G-F28: (The excess / 130) x (Person's maximum payment rate under Module A / Total of maximum payment rate of each person
--     who has parental income in common); for a relevant sibling who is an FTB child, F31(b) makes that sibling's rate 14/365 of the
--     parent's FTB maximum rate (F32), counted once (F35)
--   * s 598(2A): (Liquid assets - Maximum reserve amount) / Divisor (the first pass's inference was right; nothing to change)
-- The taper is the same for a member of a couple, applied to the 50/50 share (points 1064-E2, G2): the first pass's illustrative
-- 25c and 3.9c for couples were not the Act's. The maximum rates, free areas, limits and the parent's FTB rate stay INPUTS.
--
-- SEAT, edition and method as ssa-payments.l4 (naive, compilation C2026C00336). See NOTES.md.

§ `Social Security Act 1991 -- the first pass's lost formulas, computed`

§§ `1064-E10, Table G-2 -- the age pension tapers`

-- Point 1064-E10 (sidecar): Ordinary income excess x 0.5.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Act's income reduction per dollar of excess` MEANS 0.5

-- Table G-2 column 3 (sidecar): Assets excess x 19.5 / 250, a year, for every family situation.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Act's assets reduction per dollar of excess` MEANS 19.5 DIVIDED BY 250

-- The person's Means with the two supplied reduction rates replaced by the Act's own.
GIVEN `m` IS A Means
GIVETH A Means
`the means under the Act's tapers` MEANS
    Means WITH
        `maximum payment rate per year`         IS `m`'s `maximum payment rate per year`
        `ordinary income per year`              IS `m`'s `ordinary income per year`
        `ordinary income free area`             IS `m`'s `ordinary income free area`
        `income reduction per dollar of excess` IS `the Act's income reduction per dollar of excess`
        `value of assets`                       IS `m`'s `value of assets`
        `assets value limit`                    IS `m`'s `assets value limit`
        `assets reduction per dollar of excess` IS `the Act's assets reduction per dollar of excess`

GIVEN `m` IS A Means
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income reduced rate under the Act's taper` MEANS `the income reduced rate` (`the means under the Act's tapers` `m`)

GIVEN `m` IS A Means
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the assets reduced rate under the Act's taper` MEANS `the assets reduced rate` (`the means under the Act's tapers` `m`)

GIVEN `m` IS A Means
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the provisional annual payment rate under the Act's tapers` MEANS
    `the provisional annual payment rate` (`the means under the Act's tapers` `m`)

GIVEN `the senior` IS A Senior, `today` IS A NUMBER, `m` IS A Means
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an age pension is payable under the Act's tapers` IF
    `an age pension is payable` `the senior` `today` (`the means under the Act's tapers` `m`)

§§ `1067G-F28, F31(b) -- the parental income test with parental income in common`

-- Point 1067G-F28 (sidecar), rounded under F29 to the nearest 10 cents.
GIVEN `combined parental income` IS A NUMBER, `maintenance paid by a parent` IS A NUMBER, `parental income free area` IS A NUMBER,
      `person's maximum payment rate` IS A NUMBER, `total of maximum payment rates in common` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the F28 result` MEANS
    IF (`combined parental income` MINUS `maintenance paid by a parent`) AT MOST `parental income free area`
        OR `total of maximum payment rates in common` AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE `rounded to the nearest 10 cents`
             ((((`combined parental income` MINUS `maintenance paid by a parent`) MINUS `parental income free area`) DIVIDED BY 130)
              TIMES (`person's maximum payment rate` DIVIDED BY `total of maximum payment rates in common`))

-- F31(b), F35: a relevant sibling who is an FTB child counts at 14/365 of the parent's FTB maximum rate (F32), once only.
GIVEN `person's maximum payment rate` IS A NUMBER, `parent's FTB maximum rate` IS A NUMBER,
      `other recipients' maximum payment rates` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the F28 total with a relevant sibling` MEANS
    `person's maximum payment rate`
    PLUS ((`parent's FTB maximum rate` TIMES 14) DIVIDED BY 365)
    PLUS `other recipients' maximum payment rates`

-- The first pass's `the parental income test result`, with its F28 slot filled by the formula instead of a supplied figure.
GIVEN `combined parental income` IS A NUMBER, `maintenance paid by a parent` IS A NUMBER, `parental income free area` IS A NUMBER,
      `a parent receives a Module L payment` IS A BOOLEAN, `has parental income in common` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `person's maximum payment rate` IS A NUMBER, `total of maximum payment rates in common` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the parental income test result with F28 computed` MEANS
    `the parental income test result` `combined parental income` `maintenance paid by a parent` `parental income free area`
        `a parent receives a Module L payment` `has parental income in common`
        (`the F28 result` `combined parental income` `maintenance paid by a parent` `parental income free area`
            `person's maximum payment rate` `total of maximum payment rates in common`)
